# Real deployment state — never committed.
#
# Every pattern here sits on its own line. Git has no inline comments in a
# .gitignore: a `#` only starts a comment at the START of a line, so a trailing
# one becomes part of the pattern and the rule silently matches nothing. That
# is not hypothetical — it is what this file did until 2026-09-03, leaving
# traefik/dynamic/, .tb-installed-version and *.pem unprotected while looking
# correct, and .env/backups/ ignored only by coincidence via the root file.

# the actual secrets; .env.example is the tracked doc
.env

# database dumps contain every device credential
backups/

# rendered from dynamic.yml.in; a build product, not a source
traefik/dynamic/

# per-VPS state written by tbctl install/upgrade
.tb-installed-version

# ca-export output; regenerate with ./tbctl ca-export
*.pem
